<article class="env-definition" id="07HK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07HK">Definition <span data-tag="07HK">60.4.1</span>.</a> Let $(A, I, \gamma )$ and $(B, J, \delta )$ be divided power rings. Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. We say <em>$\delta $ is compatible with $\gamma $</em> if there exists a divided power structure $\bar\gamma $ on $J + IB$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (A, I, \gamma ) \to (B, J + IB, \bar\gamma )\quad \text{and}\quad (B, J, \delta ) \to (B, J + IB, \bar\gamma )  \]
</div>
  <p> are homomorphisms of divided power rings. </p>
</article>